>As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids runs 1951 to 2025, and October to November came in under 90% of normal in 35 of 75 years, the same count as February to March. In 2025, April to May ran 164% of normal and November to December ran 73%. So far in 2026, February to March and March to April each sit at 63% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 21487 had its driest year in 1963 at 67%.</p>"}
